INSERT INTO "session" ("id", "skill", "phase", "state", "superseded_by", "created_at", "updated_at") VALUES ('ef609fba-06b5-4d19-b550-623d9565d393', 'dpm:do', 'EPIC 02-05 COMPLETE. All three stories complete, none retired. Coverage roll-up done, retro 10 written with synthesis on all three observations. Remaining: publish, and Chris to stage the deletions and commit.', 'EPIC 02-05 "The v1 walk" 01M1C6E3XG8EVENPG8P74RHGGA is COMPLETE — the last epic of spec 02.

STORY 3 DELIVERED: end-to-end walk under real 1.18.25 in a throwaway project. Real session invoked dpm-quick, read conventions via dpm_read_shared_document, wrote session + quick + 3 criteria + observation, closed the quick; publish then commit accepted by the guard (7d2a28a); commit without publish refused with both artefacts named; hand-edited projection refused with the edit left in place; deny rule verified both directions.

DEFECT FOUND AND FIXED: README Permissions section was written in OpenCode 2''s `permissions` ARRAY. v1 refuses the whole configuration ("V2 permissions are not supported by OpenCode V1") and the session does not start. Rewritten onto v1''s singular `permission` OBJECT — `{"permission": {"skill": {"dpm-*": "allow"}, "dpm_*": "allow"}}` — verified live. permission-entries.test.js rewritten onto v1 vocabulary (key/pattern/effect) with a refusedBlocks() absence assertion; readme-v2.test.js and readme-host.test.js gained matching subjects; new tests/support/readme.js holds the shared reader.

V1 PERMISSION FACTS (read off the binary and driven live): key is `permission` (singular object). Known keys: read, edit, glob, grep, list, bash, task, external_directory, todowrite, question, webfetch, websearch, lsp, doom_loop, skill. MCP tool names are ALSO accepted as keys. Value is a bare action or {pattern: action}; last matching pattern wins within an object; per-agent permission OVERRIDES top-level. A denied skill refuses visibly with the ruleset printed; a denied TOOL is removed from the model''s tool set entirely with nothing said.

COVERAGE ROLL-UP over spec 02 (01M1BJS4H76EB2K3Z98YPNG17B): claimed this run — FR1, FR4, FR8, NFR1, NFR2, NFR4, NFR5, ENVR1, ENVR4, ENVR5, ENVX1, ENVX2, ENVX3. Already claimed — FR5. LEFT UNCLAIMED with reasons: FR2 ("Tool names, schemas and behaviour are identical under both hosts" has no bound fragment); FR3 (its first clause names a "v1 registrar" for skills that the delivered design no longer has — the `skills` config key replaced it); FR6 and FR7 (three and one unverified rows respectively: 01M1CA51ZY5R10N7KRWQ81KEGW, 01M1CA53F4RTJ75K0ZZ4Y02RDV, 01M1CA552G2FHMD2ZR2F3Q3ER5, 01M1CA587FDRSBWCZW014GZM7R); ENVR2 (no rows); ENVR3 ("each host", only v1 exercised here); NFR3 (no rows at all — its subject Config.skills.paths was superseded); ENVX4 (its check says the config files are byte-identical across a plugin load, and 1.18.25 inserts `"$schema"` into the user''s opencode.json on load — the host''s write, not the plugin''s, but the check as written does not distinguish); FR9/FR10 could, FR11-FR14 wont.

RETRO 10 01M1GPS7MS4BPFANKN7X9NA36A "The v1 walk — what the suite could not see", all three observations synthesised.

SUITE: 1179 tests, 1178 pass. The one failure is tests/plugin.test.js "a file with a shebang is executable in the index" — the index still tracks the deleted src/plugin/skills-entry.ts and tests/v1-skills.test.js. Resolves when Chris stages the deletions. typecheck, modules, skills all clean.

STILL OUTSTANDING for Chris: projection "Blocked by" inversion (src/projection/load.ts:112 parent:''source_story_id''; src/projection/templates/epic.ts:101); the develop-DPM workflow regression; reopening the packaged install is src/db/connection.ts work.', NULL, '2026-08-31T17:20:00.849Z', '2026-09-02T09:22:59.447Z');
INSERT INTO "session" ("id", "skill", "phase", "state", "superseded_by", "created_at", "updated_at") VALUES ('ef609fba-06b5-4d19-b550-623d9565d393-pivot-spec02', 'dpm:pivot', 'Complete — FR3, FR7 and ENVX4 amended; nine coverage rows retired; ENVX4''s criterion amended. Publish done.', '{"mode":"amend the record","amended_requirements":["FR3 — removed the v1 skills registrar that does not exist; mechanism is the `skills` configuration key","FR7 — replaced the dead ''unprefixed front-matter name'' premise; the prefix is in the front matter since epic 02-02","ENVX4 — the check is attribution, not byte-identity, because 1.18.25 writes $schema on load"],"amended_criteria":["01M1C9C5HZP5N85P74YW23HXGK (epic 02-01) — its hash control must attribute a difference before judging"],"retired_coverage":{"FR6":["01M1CA51ZY5R10N7KRWQ81KEGW","01M1CA53F4RTJ75K0ZZ4Y02RDV","01M1CA552G2FHMD2ZR2F3Q3ER5"],"FR7":["01M1CA587FDRSBWCZW014GZM7R"],"FR3":["01M1CQN9KJ9N6RAT5PM9JR8J7X","01M1CQNBPCF3J4NWJQRXB2XNE2","01M1CVC30NDPVK59SM0KNPQA51","01M1CQNNHBMCS6KCY44XKC3NNN"]},"decisions_by_chris":["incorporate retro 09''s two observations as the lens","apply all three amendments","leave FR6 standing and retire its three marker rows","retire FR7''s broken row","retire all four FR3 rows","amend ENVX4''s criterion despite it being completed work"],"consequence_not_flagged_before_approval":"amending a requirement''s text clears verified_at on every row bound to it, not only rows whose fragment breaks. Five standing marks were lost (FR3 x4, ENVX4 x1). None of the three was claimed, so no coverage claim was lost.","left_unclaimed_untouched":["FR2 — the clause about tool identity across hosts has no bound fragment; not a spec defect","NFR3 — subject is Config.skills.paths, which the delivered `skills` key superseded; no coverage rows","ENVR2 — no coverage rows","ENVR3 — one verified row, but its text says ''each host'' and only v1 was exercised"]}', NULL, '2026-09-03T12:09:07.717Z', '2026-09-03T12:19:02.678Z');
INSERT INTO "session" ("id", "skill", "phase", "state", "superseded_by", "created_at", "updated_at") VALUES ('ef609fba-06b5-4d19-b550-623d9565d393-retro-learn', 'dpm:retro', 'Complete — library 06 and 07 written, three observations retired at source. 10-1 left live; Chris declined the library 02 amendment.', '{"mode":"learn","promoted":[{"library":"06 check-shares-the-error","doc_type":"testing-standards","scopes":["do"],"from":["retro 10 story 3","quick 01"]},{"library":"07 the-walk-comes-first","doc_type":"architecture","scopes":["epics","spec","do"],"from":["retro 10 story 2"]}],"left_live":"retro 10 story 1 (01M1GF6D3FP7VHWV5Z8TAW8A5P) — its durable part is a refinement of library 02, offered as an amendment and declined for this run","stale_sessions":"one unfinished: 8afd89dc-...-retro-04 at ''Step 1 — gather epic 01-04''s observations'', 2026-08-30. Epic 01-04 does have retro 04, so the row is a leftover rather than work outstanding. Not deleted."}', NULL, '2026-09-03T11:19:50.822Z', '2026-09-03T11:24:09.674Z');
